==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Shadow Akira''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Inferno Akira''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Akira is a multi-purpose offensive unit. Due to Akira's immunity to weakening effects for all forms, he is useful when faced against enemies who apply this kind of debuff, most notably [[Calamary]].

==='''Normal Form'''===
In his Normal Form, he acts as an offensive crowd control unit against Aliens, which can make dealing with tough Alien bosses like [[Nimoy Bore]] much easier. Although [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer]] already exists for the purpose, Akira has a range advantage that becomes apparent on aliens Seafarer would struggle against. He has fantastic synergy with cats that excel at damaging Aliens, like [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Aphrodite]] or stacks of [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Legs Cat]]. Akira freezes the Aliens in their tracks, allowing your damage-dealers to wipe them out.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Shadow Akira is a very well-rounded damage dealer that is great in all areas. Due to his [[Strengthen]] ability, he is the best form for taking on any type of enemy, though excelling at none. This form is best used for offensive support to add to high DPS teams. He is extremely effective against resilient [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|wave attackers]] like [[Kory]] or [[Elizabeth the LVIth]]. It is possible to use wave-immune meatshields in combination with Shadow Akira to make taking out wave attackers easier.

==='''True Form'''===
Inferno Akira gains the [[Strong Against]] ability against Aliens, but in exchange for his previous form's Strengthen. Unless his expensive [[Talents]] are unlocked, Inferno Akira is only preferred over his other forms if the player is already able to keep Aliens slowed or frozen.

==='''Talents'''===
Akira requires such a massive Talent investment that sometimes it is better to use his earlier forms or resort to other alternatives, but it doesn't hurt if you're somehow able to pay for it after the more essential ones are unlocked.

'''Attack Up''' and '''[[Freeze|Freeze]]''' are obviously good, since his previous forms were reliant on them, and having all of them simultaneously does prove helpful. The '''Attack Buff''' and '''HP Buff''' are obviously very helpful on such a stat-based unit, but [[Catseye|catseyes]] must be considered first. The '''[[Survive|Survive]]''' ability has its perks for a unit with such a slow recharge and decently high range, and synergizes with his Attack Up Talent to provide an additional reposition with a guaranteed Strengthen activation.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
'''[[Surge Attack]]''' is the main thing you'll want to focus on. It's the primary reason for getting Akira to such a high level in the first place, since it functions as both piercing damage and also has the potential to double his damage per attack cycle. The Surge itself spawns at the edge of his attack, causing it to lean more towards the piercing aspect. This alone is very good, as Aliens notoriously have a lot of backliners and can be annoying with their frontliners as well. With this, Akira has the capabilities to deal with every type of Alien.

At Lv.60, assuming max Attack Buff Talents, untargeted enemies within his range will take 22k DPS if both the main attack and Surge connect, or 33k when Strengthened. These are very impressive stats and get even better when pitted against his target traits: against Alien, he deals 59,500 DPS at the absolute maximum, which is gargantuan to be sure. Even against his new target, he deals 49,500 DPS, definitely nothing to sneeze at.

To make him relevant in the lategame, Akira also gains '''Target Aku''', which gives him a new niche to unleash his monumentally overpowered DPS against. He is able to outrange a majority of common Akus, with his wave immunity countering [[Wicked Face]]/[[Deathkory]]'s main gimmicks. While he doesn't have Surge Immunity or Shield Piercing, his answer to that is his sheer damage, which can serve to counter most Akus through brute force.

Make sure you know you want Akira's Ultra Talents before investing, as it's an incredibly pricey investment and can be considered overkill in many situations where lower-performance anti-Alien/Aku nukers could achieve similar results. Regardless, the firepower speaks for itself and should be considered in any situation where you want an Aku/Alien wiped off the face of the planet.

